WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.552
A reliable model-selection process begins with the output you need, not with a famous model name.

00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:11.172
If the task is text classification or named entity recognition,

00:00:11.172 --> 00:00:18.087
an encoder-style model or a task-specific fine-tuned checkpoint may be efficient and accurate.

00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:22.712
If the task is open-ended generation, chat, or completion,

00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:27.247
a decoder-only instruction-tuned model is a more natural fit.

00:00:27.247 --> 00:00:33.802
If the task transforms one sequence into another, such as translation or summarization,

00:00:33.802 --> 00:00:37.407
an encoder-decoder model may be especially convenient.

00:00:37.407 --> 00:00:45.062
If you need vectors for semantic search, choose an embedding model that has been trained for similarity rather

00:00:45.062 --> 00:00:49.967
than simply taking any hidden state from a general model.

00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:53.862
Architecture is the first filter, not the final decision.

00:00:53.862 --> 00:00:57.052
Language, domain, model size, license, latency, privacy,

00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:01.806
and evaluation on realistic data still matter afterward.
